---
import { Font } from "astro:assets";
import { Icon } from "astro-icon/components";

import Table from "../components/Table.astro";
import TableOfContents from "../components/TableOfContents.astro";
import HeroGravity from "../components/interactive/HeroGravity.tsx";

import "../styles/global.css";
import "katex/dist/katex-swap.css";

import { Content } from "../content.mdx";

const title = "Beyond Flat Walks";
const subtitle = "Compositional Abstraction for Autoregressive Graph Generation";
const description =
  "A hierarchical graph abstraction and coarse-to-fine tokenization for autoregressive graph generation: coarsen, serialize, and decode exactly, with a standard causal transformer.";

const authors = [
  { name: "Kaiwen Bian", aff: "1,2", mark: "*" },
  { name: "Andrew H. Yang", aff: "1", mark: "*" },
  { name: "Ali Parviz", aff: "1", mark: "" },
  { name: "Gal Mishne", aff: "1", mark: "†" },
  { name: "Yusu Wang", aff: "1", mark: "†" },
];
const affiliations = ["University of California San Diego", "Salk Institute for Biological Studies"];

const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const prefix = baseUrl.endsWith("/") ? baseUrl : baseUrl + "/";

const links = [
  { name: "Paper", url: "", icon: "ri:file-pdf-2-line", soon: true },
  { name: "Code", url: "https://github.com/KevinBian107/MOSAIC", icon: "ri:github-line" },
  { name: "Hugging Face", url: "", icon: "ri:robot-2-line", soon: true },
  { name: "Citation", url: "#citation", icon: "ri:double-quotes-l" },
];

const tocSections = [
  { id: "idea", label: "Flat walks vs. hierarchy" },
  { id: "pipeline", label: "The pipeline" },
  { id: "axes", label: "Three design axes" },
  { id: "results", label: "Molecular results" },
  { id: "randomization", label: "Closing the V.U.N. gap" },
  { id: "beyond", label: "Beyond molecules" },
  { id: "alignment", label: "When hierarchy misleads" },
  { id: "context", label: "In context" },
  { id: "samples", label: "Generated samples" },
  { id: "takeaways", label: "Takeaways" },
  { id: "citation", label: "Citation" },
];
---

<!doctype html>
<html class="bg-white" lang="en" data-theme="light">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href={prefix + "favicon.svg"} />
    <meta property="og:title" content={`${title}: ${subtitle}`} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <Font cssVariable="--font-noto-sans" preload={[{ subset: "latin", style: "normal" }]} />
    <title>{`${title}: ${subtitle}`}</title>
  </head>
  <body
    class="prose prose-sm sm:prose-lg prose-zinc prose-a:text-blue-600 prose-a:no-underline prose-a:hover:underline prose-a:font-normal prose-code:bg-zinc-100 prose-code:text-zinc-800 prose-code:px-1.5 prose-code:py-0.5 prose-code:rounded prose-code:font-medium prose-code:before:content-none prose-code:after:content-none max-w-none pb-10 font-(family-name:--font-noto-sans)"
  >
    <header class="not-prose bg-zinc-950 text-white">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-[72rem] px-6 pt-14 pb-12 sm:pt-20">
        <div class="text-center">
          <h1 class="mx-auto max-w-5xl text-3xl leading-tight font-semibold sm:text-5xl">
            {title}:<br /><span class="text-zinc-300">{subtitle}</span>
          </h1>
          <div class="mx-auto mt-6 flex max-w-4xl flex-wrap justify-center gap-x-5 gap-y-1.5 text-base text-zinc-200 sm:text-lg">
            {
              authors.map((a) => (
                <span>
                  {a.name}
                  <sup class="ml-0.5 text-xs text-zinc-400">
                    {a.mark}
                    {a.aff}
                  </sup>
                </span>
              ))
            }
          </div>
          <div class="mx-auto mt-3 flex max-w-4xl flex-wrap justify-center gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-sm text-zinc-400">
            {
              affiliations.map((a, i) => (
                <span>
                  <sup class="mr-0.5">{i + 1}</sup>
                  {a}
                </span>
              ))
            }
          </div>
          <div class="mt-1.5 text-xs text-zinc-500">* Equal contribution &nbsp;·&nbsp; † Equal advising</div>
          <div class="mt-4 text-sm text-zinc-300 sm:text-base">Fortieth Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2026), Main Track</div>
          <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-2">
            {
              links.map((l) =>
                l.soon ? (
                  <span class="flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-zinc-800 px-4 py-1.5 text-sm text-zinc-400 sm:px-5 sm:py-2 sm:text-base">
                    <Icon name={l.icon} />
                    {l.name} <span class="text-xs">(coming soon)</span>
                  </span>
                ) : (
                  <a href={l.url} class="flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-white px-4 py-1.5 text-sm text-zinc-900 hover:bg-zinc-200 sm:px-5 sm:py-2 sm:text-base">
                    <Icon name={l.icon} />
                    {l.name}
                  </a>
                ),
              )
            }
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-12 grid items-start gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,1.1fr)]">
          <div>
            <h2 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-100">Abstract</h2>
            <p class="text-justify text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-zinc-300">
              Autoregressive graph generators typically linearize graphs through flat node-edge walks, which can obscure higher-order structure in large, complex
              graphs. We introduce a <b class="text-white">hierarchical graph abstraction</b> and <b class="text-white">coarse-to-fine generation pipeline</b> that
              separates coarsening, tokenization, and decoding. This exposes three design axes: community coarsening, hierarchical tokenization, and order
              randomization. Across these axes, traversal-based hierarchy consistently improves distributional and structural fidelity, while its V.U.N. cost depends
              strongly on the coarsening and randomization policy. In particular, the fidelity–V.U.N. trade-off observed under within-community randomization is
              substantially reduced when traversal order is randomized across the full hierarchy. With a fixed backbone, training recipe, and matched training time
              across five molecular and four non-molecular benchmarks, hierarchical serialization yields consistent distributional and structural gains on all
              molecular datasets, while the non-molecular results show that these gains depend on how well the supplied hierarchy aligns with structure in the target
              distribution. Together, these results characterize when and how hierarchical serialization benefits autoregressive graph generation.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <HeroGravity client:load base={baseUrl} />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <TableOfContents sections={tocSections} />
    <main class="pt-6">
      <Content components={{ table: Table }} />
    </main>
    <footer class="mx-auto mt-16 max-w-[50rem] px-6 text-center">
      <p class="prose-sm text-center text-zinc-400">
        Every animation on this page is driven by the outputs of the coarseners and tokenizers in the <a href="https://github.com/KevinBian107/MOSAIC">code
        release</a>. Built with <a href="https://research-template.roman.technology" rel="nofollow">Roman Hauksson-Neill's project page template</a>.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
